//
// Goal 1 increment W1: the NEGATIVE CONTROL for the sliding-window row.
//
// WHY THIS EXISTS. Full causal attention is a strict SUPERSET of a W=512
// window: it keeps every score the window keeps, and more. So an
// implementation that silently ignored the window and ran full causal would
// still produce plausible outputs, and the most likely bug in this change is
// exactly that -- the band is a compile-time -D on ONE object, and an object
// built without it links and runs perfectly happily. A windowed gate that
// cannot reject an unwindowed kernel is worth nothing.
//
// WHAT IT DOES. Identical shape, inputs and reference to
// run_npu2_makefile_peano_causal_window512.lit -- same 2048x2048, same seed,
// same W=512 banded FP32 reference -- but the KERNEL OBJECT is rebuilt with
// the band switched off. The Makefile emits -DWINDOW_LEN=$(WINDOW) and then
// $(EXTRA_KERNEL_FLAGS), and the last -D wins, so the flag below yields an
// unwindowed kernel while the harness still bands its reference. That run MUST
// be rejected.
//
// WHY IT IS NOT JUST AN INVERTED EXIT STATUS. "The process exited non-zero" is
// not evidence that the check discriminates: a missing PEANO_INSTALL_DIR, a
// kernel that fails to link, and an NPU that never comes up all exit non-zero
// without ever comparing anything, and a recipe that merely negated the status
// would report a passing control for every one of them. So the inversion lives
// in the driver, next to the completed comparison's statistics
// (--expect-failure), and it reports PASS only when the run reached the output
// check, that check returned FAIL, and it did so by counting mismatching
// elements. The same argument, and the same shape of fix, as
// transformer_layer/run_npu2_fault_control_peano.lit.
//
// Consequently this recipe expects the command to SUCCEED (exit 0): success
// here means "the banded gate rejected the unwindowed kernel, as required".
//
// Editing this header: lit scans the WHOLE file for directives, so naming one
// in prose -- even in a comment -- registers as a second directive and leaves
// the test UNRESOLVED. Describe them, never spell them out.
//
// REQUIRES: ryzen_ai_npu2, peano
//
// RUN: mkdir -p test_causal_window512_negative
// RUN: cd test_causal_window512_negative
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile clean
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile run PEANO_INSTALL_DIR=%PEANO_INSTALL_DIR LK=2048 LKP=64 LQ=2048 LQP=256 DK=64 DV=64 NUM_HEADS=32 NUM_KV_HEADS=8 WINDOW=512 EXTRA_KERNEL_FLAGS="-DWINDOW_LEN=0" EXTRA_PY_FLAGS="--causal --expect-failure" | FileCheck %s
//
// The reference must still have been banded (otherwise the two sides agree and
// the control is vacuous), the comparison must have run and rejected, and the
// rejection must have come from the tolerance check counting elements.
// CHECK: [window] reference band W=512
// CHECK: ERROR: Output 0 does not meet expected output.
// CHECK: failed.
// CHECK: NEGATIVE CONTROL: PASS
